{
 "rows": [
  {
   "sentence": 1,
   "start": 0.2,
   "speech_end": 5.234,
   "text": "On a bright winter day in 1919, a giant tank stood over Boston's harbor.",
   "first_word": "On",
   "end": 5.634
  },
  {
   "sentence": 2,
   "start": 5.634,
   "speech_end": 8.665,
   "text": "It held over two million gallons of sticky molasses.",
   "first_word": "It",
   "end": 9.065
  },
  {
   "sentence": 3,
   "start": 9.065,
   "speech_end": 13.743,
   "text": "For months it leaked and groaned, and the company just painted it brown to hide the leaks.",
   "first_word": "For",
   "end": 14.143
  },
  {
   "sentence": 4,
   "start": 14.143,
   "speech_end": 19.248,
   "text": "Just after noon came a sound like gunfire, as rivets flew and the tank burst open.",
   "first_word": "Just",
   "end": 19.648
  },
  {
   "sentence": 5,
   "start": 19.648,
   "speech_end": 25.633,
   "text": "A brown wave twenty-five feet high raced through the streets, crushing buildings and even bending the railway.",
   "first_word": "A",
   "end": 26.033
  },
  {
   "sentence": 6,
   "start": 26.033,
   "speech_end": 30.468,
   "text": "The cold made the molasses thick like glue, trapping people and horses.",
   "first_word": "The",
   "end": 30.868
  },
  {
   "sentence": 7,
   "start": 30.868,
   "speech_end": 36.532,
   "text": "Twenty-one people died, and sailors and firefighters worked for days as the harbor turned brown.",
   "first_word": "Twenty-one",
   "end": 36.932
  },
  {
   "sentence": 8,
   "start": 36.932,
   "speech_end": 42.547,
   "text": "In court, it came out the tank was never properly tested, leading to stricter engineering rules.",
   "first_word": "In court",
   "end": 42.947
  },
  {
   "sentence": 9,
   "start": 42.947,
   "speech_end": 46.946,
   "text": "And for decades, on hot days, the streets still smelled sweet.",
   "first_word": "And",
   "end": 47.296
  }
 ],
